    'btn.confirm.registration'=>'Registration confirmation link',
    'confirm.registration.message.member.1' => '<p>Hi,</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Thank you for sending your registration form to &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Please confirm your registration by clicking on the link below.</p>',
    'confirm.registration.message.member.2' => '<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>In case of difficulty, please copy the link and paste it in the address bar of your browser.</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>As soon as you click on the registration confirmation link above, we will send to your email address an email containing your various login details and your system-generated password. You will be asked to replace this system password later with a password that will be personal to you.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>With our best regards</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Investir en Australie Team</p>',
    'confirm.registration.message.seller.rep.1' => '<p>Hi,</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Thank you for sending your Real Estate Professional registration form to &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Please confirm your registration by clicking on the link below.</p>',
    'confirm.registration.message.seller.rep.2' => '<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>In case of difficulty, please copy the link and paste it in the address bar of your browser.</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>As soon as you click on the registration confirmation link above, we will send to your email address an email containing your various login details and your system-generated password. You will be asked to replace this system password later with a password that will be personal to you.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>With our best regards</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Investir en Australie Team</p>',
    'confirm.registration.message.seller.slp.1' => '<p>Hi,</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Thank you for sending your Non-Professional Legal Person registration form to &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Please confirm your registration by clicking on the link below.</p>',
    'confirm.registration.message.seller.slp.2' => '<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>In case of difficulty, please copy the link and paste it in the address bar of your browser.</p> <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>As soon as you click on the registration confirmation link above, we will send to your email address an email containing your various login details and your system-generated password. You will be asked to replace this system password later with a password that will be personal to you.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>With our best regards</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Investir en Australie Team</p>',
    'registration.confirmed.member'=>'<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Hi <b>:name</b>, </p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>We welcome you as a Member of the &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal. We will most often use the abbreviation IEA to refer to the &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; system or portal. For a first approach, the section &quot;How the Investing in Australia portal works&quot; on the home page offers you a synthetic view of the operations that you can perform via the portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>You now have an IEA Portal Member account. We will communicate to you and remind you below of your username and password which will allow you to connect to the portal using the &quot;Connection&quot; tab at the top of the home page. The password provided to you is randomly generated by the system. It is recommended that you replace it with a personal and secret password. Your personal password that you will register must be at least 8 characters long and contain at least 1 lower case letter, 1 upper case letter, 1 number and 1 special character.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Your username and password are as follows:</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>- <b>Registration number : :immat</b><br/>- <b>Login : :login</b><br/>- <b>E-mail adress : :email</b><br/>- <b>Password : :password</b><br/></p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Only the email address and password will be required for you to connect as a Member, which will allow you to access your profile, your personal account and your personal dashboard through the &quot;Account&quot; tab in the toolbar.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>In your profile you will find, throughout your practice on the portal, the various useful information, such as your affiliation situations with &quot;Local Partner Agencies&quot; and &quot;Francophone Australian Agencies&quot;. You can communicate with these agencies via the portal&rsquo;s internal messaging :</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>The &quot;Local Partner Agencies&quot; (APL) </p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;> These are the agencies that are responsible for conducting real estate transaction files in Australia. During his search for goods it is possible for the Member to contact various AFA for information. However, once he has decided to initiate a specific purchase transaction, he will be asked to select a particular AFA who will then be entrusted with the conduct of the transaction. </p> <p class=&quot; p-10px -tb &quot;> The use of an AFA is completely free for the Member.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Exchanges with AFAs are protected by anonymity, which prohibits communicating email or telephone contacts. This rule is essential to protect the Member from untimely solicitations from agencies. If a party breaks this rule, their message is automatically scrambled by the system. This rule of anonymity is lifted once the Member has initiated a purchase transaction.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Transactions carried out through the IEA portal do not give rise to any payment of intervention fees to the IEA portal. Only the seller or his lawyer (solicitor) has to pay the purchase price of the property, taxes and public costs related to the purchase, as well as the emoluments of your own solicitor. We invite you to browse the blog articles of the portal and our &quot;{Investor&rsquo;s Guide}&quot; which will provide you with essential information relating to the main aspects of an investment of this type.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>When you have started a purchase operation, the portal will bring you, as needed, the contacts of French-speaking Australian professionals whose services you may need or useful. </p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot; > We would like to thank you for the trust you have placed in us by registering as a Member on the IEA portal. Although it is still very limited, it is intended to cover all eight States and Territories of Australia. </p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;> Wishing you good navigation and in expressing the wish that you find a property that will meet your expectations.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>With our cordial greetings</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb text-right&quot;>The team &quot;Investir en Australie&quot;</p>',
    'registration.confirmed.seller.rep'=>'<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Hi</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>We welcome you as a Real Estate Professional Seller of &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal. We will most often use the abbreviation IEA to refer to the &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; system or portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>You now have an IEA Portal Real Estate Professional Seller account. We will communicate to you and remind you below of your username and password which will allow you to connect to the portal using the &quot;Connection&quot; tab at the top of the home page. The password provided to you is randomly generated by the system. It is recommended that you replace it with a personal and secret password. Your personal password that you will register must be at least 8 characters long and contain at least 1 lower case letter, 1 upper case letter, 1 number and 1 special character.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Your references, username and password are as follows:</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>- <b>Reference number : :immat</b><br/>- <b>Login : :login</b><br/>- <b>E-mail adress : :email</b><br/>- <b>Password : :password</b><br/></p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Only the email address and password will be required for you to connect as a Seller, which will allow you to access your profile, your personal account and your personal dashboard through the &quot;Account&quot; tab in the toolbar.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;><b>We wish to alert you to the confidentiality that should be respected regarding access to your account, in particular with regard to the possibility of publication and modification of programs/products/properties. We therefore recommend that you kindly only give access to your account to a limited number of trusted people in your company. However, we have taken security measures into account when registering programs/products/properties to ensure, as long as it is possible to do so, that your company is the author of the registration.</b></p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;> IEA portal is targeting people in Francophone countries and territories interested in or wishing to invest in Australia. When you register your programs/products/properties in English, they are automatically translated into French for complying with the language of the target markets. This means that the programs/products/properties you publish on IEA portal will be able to be displayed in French and likely to be seen and understood by the 250+ millions French speaking people around the world, AT ABSOLUTELY NO COST FOR YOU.</p> <p class=&quot; p-10px -tb &quot;>The buyers are called IEA portal&rsquo;s &quot;<b>Members</b>&quot;. The concept of IEA system intends to create a massive worldwide Francophone selling network for bringing your programs/products/properties to the Member&rsquo;s doorstep, wherever in the world that Member may live.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Because you are a real estate professional seller (builder or developer), your residential programs/products/properties are necessarily new products. You know that the Australian foreign direct investment control regulations implemented by the Foreign Investment Review Board (FIRB) only authorize the sale of NEW residential properties to non-resident foreigners, with the exception of very rare cases of &quot;Integrated Tourism Resorts&quot;. In addition, there are also several different rules that apply to other types of foreign investment.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>This restriction applies to most IEA portal Members from Francophone countries and territories. This is the reason why you have already been asked to undertake to publish on this portal only properties that can be sold to non-resident foreigners, subject to prior approval from the FIRB.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;><u>How IEA system works</u></p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;>The function of IEA system is to provide Australian sellers with international Francophone buyers and to provide its own buying Members, to the extent possible, with service in French from the start to the end of a transaction. IEA system therefore works with : <br/>- sellers who agree to publish their properties, free of charge, on the portal;<br/>- Experienced Agences Francophones Australiennes - AFA (Australian Francophone Agencies) to whom are entrusted the properties sales operations;<br/>- an international network of Agences Partenaires Locales – APL (Local Partner Agencies) established in Francophone countries and territories, who inform, advise and guide Members in their decisions to make investments in Australia.</p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;>The remuneration of IEA portal takes the form of a &quot;Commission de Présentation de Clientèle&quot; – CPC (Client Introduction Commission) paid by the AFA who took charge of the purchasing Member&rsquo;s file. IEA portal then remunerates the APL who the purchasing Member has called upon.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;><u>How to publish Properties on the portal</u></p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>You will be asked to register yourself your properties using the appropriate IEA portal procedure which can be accessed in your dashboard &quot;Register Properties&quot; heading and either &quot;Add a Program&quot; or &quot;Add a Stand-Alone Product&quot;.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Stand-Alone Products are properties that are not linked to a program.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>There are two levels in a program : the &quot;Program&quot; itself and its associated &quot;Products&quot;.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>- A &quot;Program&quot; is a multi-units complex. It can be an apartment building, a residential villas &quot;village&quot;, a townhouse residences, a housing estate or a housing development… You will be asked to mention the lowest and the highest prices in the Program for the ranking of the properties when a Member is browsing the programs with a minimum and a maximum price.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>- Each program contains a number of included types of units called associated &quot;Products&quot;, each with similar features that a buyer will get. In that case, an associated &quot;Product&quot; belongs necessarily to a &quot;Program&quot;. So IEA portal procedure will allow Products to be registered within the Program they belong to. You will be asked to mention the lowest and the highest price for each product for the buyer&rsquo;s information.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>For a better understanding of &quot;Programs&quot; and &quot;Products&quot;, let&rsquo;s take an example. You build a 12-storey residential building that you call &quot;The Lake Residences&quot;. In this building there are 10 types of units identified by a letter, from A to J. All units of the same type are identical, stacked from the first to the twelfth floor. There are therefore 120 units for sale.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>To register this building, you will first register the &quot;Program&quot; itself under the name &quot;The Lake Residences&quot;. To enable your program to be identified in Internet user&rsquo;s searches, you will indicate in this program as a minimum price the price of the cheapest unit in the entire program, and as a maximum price the price of the most expensive unit in the entire program.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>After registering the program, you will register each one of the types of units (the &quot;Products&quot;) that make it up (units A, B, C, D…). For each type of unit you will indicate as the minimum price the price of the cheapest unit of this type of unit and as the maximum price the price of the most expensive unit of this type of unit.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>For your information, you must know that IEA portal standard for sales commission rates is 5% + GST and its Administrator will check the proposed rate before approving the property publication on the portal. However special attention will be paid to properties significantly above the standard market. Most often, sellers offer at least a 6% + GST rate when it comes to international sales to take into account the higher prospecting costs, which is the case for IEA portal clientele. Properties offering a sales commission rate above 6% + GST get a special &quot;put forward&quot; display treatment.  The above rates are subjects to modifications by the Administrator.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>IEA portal values too much the Sellers, who are our partners who bring in properties for sale, to accept the idea that the value of their properties could be tarnished by repetitive identical publishings. We do not want IEA portal to appear as a &quot;Big Bazaar&quot; like many others, where a same property could be equally published by multiple agencies. On the other hand we want to make it simple for the public to find &quot;their property&quot;, which could be more difficult with too many times the same properties appearing on the portal. Therefore we have set up the following principles :<br/>- the owner has priority to advertise, but can waive their priority right to publish and give permission to one real estate agency to do so;<br/>- a property can only be published on the site by a single advertiser (owner or agency)</br>- an agency wishing to publish a property must obtain the prior consent of the owner. IEA portal sends to the owner&rsquo;s email address a message looking for the owner&rsquo;s confirmation that they waive their priority right to publish and that they agree to the agency doing the publication itself.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Before the program to be validated by the portal Administrator and publicly displayed on IEA portal you will have to deliver to the internal IEA system Australian real estate agency :ieaagencyname a mandatory official sales mandate.</p>
    <p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>When a Member decides to buy a property they are asked to sign a search mandate to an agency they must select among the IEA&rsquo;s list of AFAs located in the same city, who will then be the agency managing the sale, together with the buyer&rsquo;s solicitor.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>If sometimes it is an isolated, stand-alone product, which is not part of a Program, then the product will be registered as a &quot;Product&quot;, specifically as a &quot;Stand-Alone Product&quot;.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Please remember that there are no fees attached to properties registration on IEA portal and no fees on sales apart the sales commissions you will pay to the AFAs in case of a sale. So feel free to register on IEA portal as many properties as you wish, free of charges.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>The whole IEA team wishes you a warm welcome and expresses the wish for a profitable mutual co-operation.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb text-right&quot;>Yours sincerely</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb text-right&quot;>Investir en Australie</p>',
    'registration.confirmed.seller.slp'=>'<p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Hi</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>We welcome you as a &quot;Non-Professional Legal Person&quot; Seller of &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; portal. We will most often use the abbreviation IEA to refer to the &quot;Investir en Australie&quot; system or portal.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>You now have an IEA Portal &quot;Non-Professional Legal Person&quot; seller account. We will communicate and remind you below of your username and password which will allow you to connect to the portal using the &quot;Connection&quot; tab at the top of the home page. The password provided to you is randomly generated by the system. It is recommended that you replace it with a personal and secret password. Your personal password that you will register must be at least 8 characters long and contain at least 1 lower case letter, 1 upper case letter, 1 number and 1 special character.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Your references, username and password are as follows:</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>- <b>Reference number : :immat</b><br/>- <b>Login : :login</b><br/>- <b>E-mail adress : :email</b><br/>- <b>Password : :password</b><br/></p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;>Only the email address and password will be required for you to connect as a Seller, which will allow you to access your profile, your personal account and your personal dashboard through the &quot;Account&quot; tab in the toolbar.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-b&quot;><b>We wish to alert you to the confidentiality that should be respected regarding access to your account, in particular with regard to the possibility of publication and modification of properties. We therefore recommend that you kindly only give access to your account to a limited number of trusted people in your company. However, we have taken security measures into account when registering properties to ensure, as long as it is possible to do so, that your company is the author of the registration.</b></p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;> IEA portal is targeting people in Francophone countries and territories interested in or wishing to invest in Australia. When you register in English your properties you want to sell, they are automatically translated into French for complying with the language of the target markets. This means that the properties you publish on IEA portal will be able to be displayed in French and likely to be seen and understood by the 250+ millions French speaking people around the world, AT ABSOLUTELY NO COST FOR YOU.</p> <p class=&quot; p-10px -tb &quot;>The buyers are called IEA portal&rsquo;s &quot;<b>Members</b>&quot;. The concept of IEA system intends to create a massive worldwide Francophone selling network for bringing your properties to the Member&rsquo;s doorstep, wherever in the world that Member may live.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>According to Australian laws about foreign direct investment applied by the Foreign Investment Review board (FIRB), only new residential properties can be sold to non-residents foreigners who make IEA portal&rsquo;s target market. Therefore, if they are residential, your properties must be new, with the exception of very rare cases of &quot;Integrated Tourism Resorts&quot;. In addition, there are also several different rules that apply to other types of foreign investment.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>This is the reason why you have already been asked to undertake to publish on this portal only properties that can be sold to non-resident foreigners, subject to prior approval from the FIRB.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;><u>How IEA system works</u></p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;>The function of IEA system is to provide Australian sellers with international Francophone buyers and to provide its own buying Members, to the extent possible, with service in French from the start to the end of a transaction. IEA system therefore works with : <br/>- sellers who agree to publish their properties, free of charge, on the portal;<br/>- Experienced Agences Francophones Australiennes - AFA (Australian Francophone Agencies) to whom are entrusted the properties sales operations;<br/>- an international network of Agences Partenaires Locales – APL (Local Partner Agencies) established in Francophone countries and territories, who inform, advise and guide Members in their decisions to make investments in Australia.</p> <p class=&quot; p-10px-tb &quot;>The remuneration of IEA portal takes the form of a &quot;Commission de Présentation de Clientèle&quot; – CPC (Client Introduction Commission) paid by the AFA who took charge of the purchasing Member&rsquo;s file. IEA portal then remunerates the APL who the purchasing Member has called upon.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;><u>How to publish Properties on the portal</u></p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>You will be asked to register yourself your own properties using the appropriate IEA portal procedure which can be accessed in your dashboard &quot;Register Properties&quot; heading and either &quot;Add a Program&quot; or &quot;Add a Stand-Alone Product&quot;. Your properties being likely to be isolated, stand-alone properties, they will be registered as &quot;Stand-Alone Products&quot;</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>For your information, you must know that IEA portal standard for sales commission rates is 5% + GST and its Administrator will check the proposed rate before approving the property publication on the portal. However special attention will be paid to properties significantly above the standard market. Most often, sellers offer at least a 6% + GST rate when it comes to international sales to take into account the higher prospecting costs, which is the case for IEA portal clientele. Properties offering a sales commission rate above 6% + GST get a special &quot;put forward&quot; display treatment.  The above rates are subjects to modifications by the Administrator.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Before the property to be validated by the portal Administrator and publicly displayed on IEA portal you will have to deliver to the internal IEA system Australian real estate agency :ieaagencyname a mandatory official sales mandate.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>When a Member decides to buy a property they are asked to sign a search mandate to an agency they must select among the IEA&rsquo;s list of AFAs located in the same city, who will then be the agency managing the sale, together with the buyer&rsquo;s solicitor.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>Please remember that there are no fees attached to properties registration on IEA portal and no fees on sales apart the sales commissions you will pay to the AFAs in case of a sale. So feel free to register on IEA portal as many properties as you wish, free of charges.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb&quot;>The whole IEA team wishes you a warm welcome and expresses the wish for a profitable mutual co-operation.</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb text-right&quot;>Yours sincerely</p><p class=&quot;p-10px-tb text-right&quot;>Investir en Australie</p>',
